                                "sense_id": "34ffad8c-3ab9-32c2-aa5d-7daf63fec166",
                                "text": "If he made transcendental distinctions, he fortified himself by drawing all his illustrations from sources disdained by orators and polite conversers; from mares and puppies; from pitchers and soup-ladles; from cooks and criers; the shops of potters, horse-doctors, butchers, and fishmongers."
